# Security identity of the active VFS target.
#
# Platform-specific types and functions are exposed by the submodules below.
#
# ## Modules
#
# | Module                                   | Description                       |
# | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
# | [`security.unix`](security.unix)       | POSIX.1e ACLs and uid/gid lookups |
# | [`security.nfs4`](security.nfs4)       | NFSv4 ACLs                        |
# | [`security.macos`](security.macos)     | macOS extended ACLs and UUIDs     |
# | [`security.windows`](security.windows) | Windows security descriptors      |

# Returns the current target user's name.
#
# This is the real user ID's name on Unix, or the access token's user SID's
# name on Windows.
#
# ## Returns
#
# [`Str`](std.Str)
#
# ## Example
#
# ```
# echo "running as $(user_name())"
# ```
pub def user_name()
  throw nil
